{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"halfalive-smoky-mara","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"pydantic-ai-slim 2.x is current upstream (2.68.0 on 2026-11-12; 85 2.x releases), while every rebar extra pins `>=1,<2` (pyproject.toml lines 133, 150, 315, 318) and 32 modules under src/rebar import pydantic_ai. Dependabot's weekly uv run could not resolve the major bump, so eagleeyed-lexical-midge set .github/dependabot.yml to ignore pydantic-ai-slim semver-major updates until this migration lands (the same arrangement as mcp and bared-nickel-insect).\n\nScope to plan: read the 2.x changelog for breaking changes affecting rebar's runner, structured output, Bedrock/Anthropic providers, tool calling and model settings; raise the pins; adapt call sites; keep the provider-parity and runner test suites green; then remove the semver-major ignore from .github/dependabot.yml.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] rebar resolves and passes `make verify` on pydantic-ai-slim 2.x, and the pins in pyproject.toml allow 2.x.\n- [ ] The pydantic-ai-slim semver-major ignore is removed from .github/dependabot.yml.","id":"09f3-de69-a8ca-4f5f","parent_id":"","priority":3,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Migrate rebar from pydantic-ai-slim 1.x to 2.x"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1794480001477917406,"uuid":"172f4565-7f14-4834-9346-279b8cc3b926"}